      "writtenOn": "2016-04-12T18:11:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s how it works by the spec. A CA may not be able to generate the cert right away so it responds with just a URL at which the cert will eventually be available - clients need to poll in that case.\n\n\"If the certificate is available at the time of the response, it is provided in the body of the response. If the CA has not yet issued the certificate, the body of this response will be empty. The client should then send a GET request to the certificate URI to poll for the certificate.\"\nhttps://ietf-wg-acme.github.io/acme/#rfc.section.6.5\n\nSo, your comment made be realize it\u0027s probably a good idea to poll here as well, just like with FetchCert which accepts cancellable context.\n\nAdded polling.",
      "parentUuid": "8b3abef4_da2f65d0",
      "revId": "05099fd37bddfb17d196c11d52ca2363aedfb017",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
